 "content": "In Herman Melville's *Moby-Dick*, Ishmael, a restless sailor, joins the whaling ship *Pequod* under the command of the obsessive Captain Ahab. Ahab lost his leg to the white whale Moby Dick and is consumed by revenge, offering a gold doubloon to whoever first sights the beast. As the *Pequod* voyages across the oceans, encountering other ships and enduring omens and storms, Ahab's mania isolates him from his crew and the practical concerns of the whaling trade. Despite warnings\u2014from first mate Starbuck, and from the captain of the *Rachel*, whose son was lost to the whale\u2014Ahab presses on. The *Pequod* finally confronts Moby Dick, and after three days of battle, the whale destroys the ship, drowning Ahab and all aboard except Ishmael, who alone survives to tell the tale."
